{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f98f3c8fee723f1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: -1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and certification submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic assembles the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model\n36\tserving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results for\n37\tevery serving-stack image in scope (KServe components, serving data plane, and\n38\tPlatform Operator) — and submits it through the security review board to the\n39\texternal accredited certification lab.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Consolidate the per-image crypto module inventories, build attestations, and\n44\t  FIPS test results produced by the serving-stack image remediations into a\n45\t  single compliance evidence package.\n46\t- Drive the package through the required security review board milestone\n47\t  sign-offs.\n48\t- Submit the package to the external accredited certification lab and record\n49\t  the submission confirmation.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The evidence package contains the module inventory, build attestations, and\n54\t  test results covering every serving-stack image in scope, with no gaps.\n55\t- The package passes the required security review board milestone reviews.\n56\t- The complete package is submitted to the accredited certification lab with\n57\t  all required artifacts and milestone sign-offs, and the submission\n58\t  confirmation is recorded.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks / Notes\n61\t\n62\t- The accredited lab's historical turnaround is six to nine months, and the\n63\t  review board meets on a fixed cadence; both are externally controlled and\n64\t  cannot be compressed by engineering effort. They gate the certification\n65\t  outcome and the certification date, not this epic's deliverable (a complete,\n66\t  submitted package).\n67\t- Acceptance into the lab's review queue is granted by the external lab, not\n68\t  by this epic's work: it is the expected follow-on to a complete, compliant\n69\t  submission, and is tracked here as an acceptance expectation rather than an\n70\t  acceptance criterion.\n71\t- Re-split trigger: if module-inventory and test-result assembly outgrows\n72\t  roughly one sprint of effort, split the assembly work from the\n73\t  submission/review-board coordination work.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-2 (P0): a compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n78\t  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security\n79\t  review board to the external certification lab.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ad9b1d333136ecc","agent_id":"a8dc2f04d6e19c874","session_id":"349a626c-8ce8-443f-b6d9-a34677df2f24","uuid":"96a10dfa-4ad2-4c4e-91a4-41331029ffed","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:46:51.184Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f98f3c8fee723f1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
